"…Saving…MenuWorkbookLumen & Loom Studio1. Identity System1. DefinitionOrganisationLumen & Loom Studio LtdPrivate Company Limited by Shares (Ltd)Unit 4, Hackney Wick Maker Yard, 92 Wallis RoadLondon E9 5LNCore Market PositioningWorkers / ProfessionalsStartups & SMBsB2C: DirectB2B: DirectCreation & ExpressionFounders & OwnershipMaya ChenOliver GrantPriya ShahRegistrations & ExpensesRegistrationsExpenses2. PurposeMission &VisionTo bring slow, handmade craft back into everyday homes: making beautiful, durable textiles from responsibly sourced materials, paying fair prices along our supply chain, and teaching people the skills to make and repair for themselves.By 2030, to be London's best-known independent weaving studio: a self-sustaining team of eight makers, a collection stocked by twenty UK independent retailers, a waiting list for our workshops, and a verified low-carbon supply chain from sheep to sofa.Values &Principles1. Craft over speed2. Honesty about materials and prices3. Care for people and planet4. Openness: share skills, not secrets5. Community before scale1. Every yarn we use is traceable to its farm or mill.2. We pay our makers and suppliers a London Living Wage or better.3. We repair anything we have made, for life.4. We never discount to clear stock; we make to order instead.5. We decide by consensus of the three founders on anything that affects people or materials.Philosophy &ManifestoWe believe the things we live with shape how we live. A well-made textile, repaired and kept for decades, teaches us to care for what we own. Our work is a small, practical argument for slowness: fewer, better things, made close to home by people you can meet.We stand for things made slowly and kept for a lifetime. We stand for knowing who made your cushion and where the wool came from. We stand against throwaway homeware, hidden supply chains and craft reduced to a style. Come and see how it's made. Better still, come and make it with us.‹PagesIntroductionIdentity Syst