[fields] Clarity over cleverness | Reliability in everything we deliver | Honesty about what AI can and cannot do | Respect for client data and privacy | Long-term partnership | We map and measure a workflow before we automate it. | We quote fixed prices and agree the scope in writing. | We build on the client's existing tools wherever we can. | Every automation that affects clients or money has a named person who checks it. | We document every build so the client could run it without us. | We never put client data into a new tool without the client's written approval. | We turn down work we cannot deliver well."
`;

exports[`Quillfield Automation > Identity System › 3. Legal Entity 1`] = `
"…Saving…MenuWorkbookQuillfield Automation1. Identity System1. DefinitionOrganisationQuillfield AutomationSole Proprietorship120 Clinton Street, Suite 3RBrooklyn 11201Early PositioningStartups & SMBsDirectProductivity & EfficiencyFounders & OwnershipJordan EllisRegistrations & ExpensesRegistrationsExpenses2. PurposeMission &VisionTo give small professional firms back the hours they lose to repetitive admin. Many small firms spend a large part of each week copying data between tools, chasing documents and writing the same emails again and again. Large consultancies do not serve them, and ready-made AI tools rarely fit how they work. We build reliable, well-documented automations around the tools a firm already uses, so its people can spend their time on client work. This matters because small firms compete on care and expertise, not on admin capacity.A future in which every small professional firm can use automation and AI as safely and confidently as a large one. Ten years from now, Quillfield is a trusted name for practical automation among small firms across the north-east United States: a small team of automation specialists, a library of proven and well-documented workflows, and hundreds of client firms whose staff spend their days on skilled work. Success means clients who stay for years, recommend us to their peers and never feel locked in.Values &Principles1. Clarity over cleverness2. Reliability in everything we deliver3. Honesty about what AI can and cannot do4. Respect for client data and privacy5. Long-term partnership1. We map and measure a workflow before we automate it.2. We quote fixed prices and agree the scope in writing.3. We build on the client's existing tools wherever we can.4. Every automation that affects clients or money has a named person who checks it.5. We document every build so the client could run it without us.6. We never put client data into a new tool without the client's written approval.7. We turn down work we cannot deliver well.Philosophy &ManifestoWe believe technology should serve people's working day, not reshape it around a tool. The best automation is quiet: it removes a chore, works every time and is easy to understand. We would rather automate one workflow well than ten badly. And we believe clients should always own, and understand, what we build for them.We stand for small firms having the same smart tools as large ones. We stand for automation that people understand, own and trust. We stand against hype, black-box systems and contracts that lock clients in. We stand against software that replaces people's judgement without anyone checking it. Everything we build exists for one reason: to give people back time for the work they chose their profession for.‹PagesIntroductionIdentity System: definedBack
[fields] "
`;

